# MO-1306 Phase 3B-R2 independent release artifact certification

**Corrected artifact certification passes; releaseReady=true within Phase 3B-R2.** Undici is NOT_REACHABLE_IN_FROZEN_USAGE; fast-xml-parser is REACHABLE_NOT_ATTACKER_CONTROLLED. No discretionary risk acceptance is made and neither frozen Action pin is changed. Separate Phase 3A-R and Phase 3D release gates remain unresolved.

The decision comes from this review's independently checked pinned sources, exact upstream module comparisons, library call paths, input origins and bounded offline witnesses. Historical conclusions remain visible and unchanged. In particular, the reproduced XML count bypass is a real parser-contract defect. Its vulnerable input in this workflow is hosted-service response XML, not repository or artifact bytes. Ordinary service errors are code-reachable without compromise; control of malicious XML requires a failure in the explicit hosted endpoint/service/transport trust boundary.

The [Undici maintainer advisory](https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-35p6-xmwp-9g52) and [fix](https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/6ea54ef8c4051e95bb68c89d4a5c9274fe6fbb4b) establish the affected reused-socket mechanism. The [XML maintainer advisory](https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser/security/advisories/GHSA-8gc5-j5rx-235r), exact5.4.1 sources and [fix](https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser/commit/bd26122c838e6a55e7d7ac49b4ccc01a49999a01) establish the missing count. Authoritative source snapshots, hashes and acquisition records are retained. The detailed [XML review](../repositories/cca-conformance/docs/mo1306-phase3b-r2-xml.md) explains its dataflow and transport qualification.

Evidence root: `repositories/cca-conformance/evidence/mo1306/phase3b-r2/`. The independent canonical receipt and closed provenance are generated only after required evidence checks. Package bytes and all historical worktrees remain unchanged.

